Package: spds
Type: Package
Title: Spatial-statistical downscaling with uncertainty quantification
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2025-01-05
Author: Xiaotian Zheng
Maintainer: Xiaotian Zheng <xiaotianzheng42@gmail.com>
Description: Downscale coarse-resolution data to fine resolutions using a GPB (Gaussian process over Basic Areal Units).
             Reference:  Zheng, X., Cressie, N., Clarke, D. A., McGeoch, M. A., and Zammit-Mangion, A. (2025).
                         Spatial-statistical downscaling with uncertainty quantification in biodiversity modelling.
             This fork adds a basis-function variant (gpbau_new / predict.gpbau_new) in which the spatial
             process is represented by r basis functions with coefficients alpha ~ N(0, sigmasq * K_psi),
             giving a block covariance K_B = W_B phi(S)' K_psi phi(S) W_B'. Because the fine-scale variation
             term delta(S) is assumed zero, K_B has rank at most min(M_D, r); the number of basis functions
             must therefore satisfy r >= M_D (number of coarse blocks) for the model to be well posed.
